<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Q3 GDP seen up 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Q3 GDP seen up 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch gross domestic product (GDP) is expected to show real growth of 3.0 percent in the third quarter of 1996 compared to the same period in 1995, according to Dutch bank economists.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT   Date  Period   Indicator	   Consensus  Range    Pvs</p>
<p> 0830  28/11 Q3	 GDP (Q3 vs Q3 95) +3.0 pct   2.6/3.0 +2.8</p>
<p> 0830  28/11 Q3	 GDP (Q3 vs Q2 96) +0.4 pct  0.15/0.5 +1.3</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
